  "rationale": "`Sources::list` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs#impl[Sources]/fn[list]` matches the required signature. It is `pub async fn list(&self, scope: &SourceScope) -> Result<Vec<PathBuf>, SourceError>` in `impl Sources`. It delegates to the provider's `list` and maps each `ResourceId` to `PathBuf::from(id.location)`. `Sources` wraps `SourceAnalysis<LocalSources>`. `LocalSources` implements `SourceProvider` with `type Error = SourceError`, so the `?` yields `SourceError`. The trait method `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#trait[SourceProvider]/fn[list]` is the delegation interface, and it takes `&SourceScope`. I found no structural gap.",
